{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The `upsert_command` command creates or updates a backend command definition within a specified library and control, validating its language, parameters, and return type before persisting the associated Rust code and imports. Upon successful storage, it automatically triggers a compilation process to verify the code's integrity and returns a status object indicating success or detailing any compilation errors. CONTRACT: `code_body` is the FUNCTION BODY ONLY — the system generates `pub fn <cmd>(<params>) -> <return_type>` around it. Never include a fn signature in code_body. Declared params are in scope as named variables of their Rust types. The final expression of code_body must be a value of the declared return_type. Put use statements in `imports`. Updating an existing command preserves its meta and impl records' readers/writers (its security gating); a new command starts admin-only until set_groups grants access. JAVASCRIPT/TYPESCRIPT (lang `javascript` or `typescript`): code_body is the body of a JavaScript function (async when it uses await) whose parameters are the declared params, in order; it ends with `return <value>`, not a final expression. A typescript body may carry type annotations. `imports` holds ES `import` lines for npm packages installed in node_modules next to data/, or for another JavaScript/TypeScript command as `flowlang:<lib>/<ctl>/<cmd>` (its function is the default export; what its imports field exports comes along) - bundled with esbuild; there is no require, process, Buffer or Node built-in. The compile step checks syntax (and bundles imports); run check_js afterwards for the type check.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::unique_session_id::unique_session_id;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::data;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse crate::dev::dev::compile::compile;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","